{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima feels like a natural next choice after 10.000 Days because I want to explore more of Tool's heavy, progressive music.",
    "Ghost Reveries and City of Evil appeal through heavy riffs, intricate arrangements, and melody, while Every Man For Himself connects with my earlier interest in The Reason."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Year Zero's industrial electronic direction does not satisfy my current desire for guitar-driven rock and metal, even though heaviness connects it loosely with my listening.",
    "I cannot confidently connect Demonic or Iv with my interests from their titles alone; passing on them reflects uncertainty rather than a definite dislike of their music."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in heavy music seems to have been treated too broadly: heaviness alone does not capture the riffs, melody, and progressive arrangements I want.",
    "My broader rock listening explains some choices, but a general rock connection makes Pearl Jam or Decemberunderground less compelling than the Tool and Opeth albums today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent interest in 10.000 Days makes further exploration of Tool especially appealing right now.",
    "My listening includes both melodic rock and heavier music, but today I prioritize albums that combine strong guitar work with elaborate arrangements over familiar rock hooks alone."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations capture my rock and metal interests, but my strongest choices depend on progressive arrangements, guitar-driven heaviness, and specific connections to albums I have explored."
}"}
